xnu: fix the Adreno clock waits and make the read-only probe hang-safe

Three deviations from the vendor/Pong clk_branch_wait and clk_rcg2_set_rate
semantics, all of which turn a healthy GPU into a false failure:

  - GCC 0x81004 in HWCG mode keeps CLK_OFF set and reports bits0..1==3; the
    vendor treats that as on. 0179 polled bit31 and declared it halted.
  - GPUCC 0x911c is the branch the vendor marks delayed: enable, wait 10us, do
    not poll. 0179 polled it and failed.
  - A root mux whose update bit is still set must not be reprogrammed; 0179
    skipped that check and would have dropped its rate setting silently.

The probe also reads in a hang-safe order now: gpucc and gmu_ao (CX/AO, on at
boot) first, then gmu, and kgsl's GX domain only behind sweetadreno_kgsl=1,
because an MMIO read of a collapsed GX domain hangs the NoC with no output.
Nothing is written in the M1 path; the power sequence stays behind
sweetadreno_power=1.

The chipid is the DT constant 0x7030002, not a register, and the log says so
instead of implying the probe could read it.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -73,6 +73,34 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Branch enable + wait, exactly the vendor clk_branch_wait semantics:
+ * CLK_OFF clear (bit31=0) or the NOC FSM state 0x2..., the HWCG-mode shortcut
+ * on GCC 0x81004, and no halt poll at all for the one branch the vendor marks
+ * delayed (the 10us settle is all it waits for). */
+static int
+sweet_adreno_branch(volatile void *blk, uint32_t off, int delayed)
+{
+	uint32_t v;
+
+	sweet_adreno_rmw(blk, off, 1, 1);
+	delay(delayed ? 10 : 5);
+	if (delayed) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < 200; i++) {
+		v = sweet_adreno_rd(blk, off);
+		if (!(v & 0x80000000) || (v & 0xf0000000) == 0x20000000) {
+			return 0;
+		}
+		if (off == 0x81004 && (v & 3) == 3) {
+			return 0;      /* HWCG mode: vendor skips halt polling */
+		}
+		delay(1);
+	}
+	IOLog("SWEET ADRENO: branch %#x halted (%#x)\n", off, sweet_adreno_rd(blk, off));
+	return -1;
+}
